    <selectionEntry id="0164-f47e-2789-9154" name="Tomb Spyders" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="unit">
      <rules>
        <rule id="5289-117d-d3d6-efa7" name="Tomb Spyders" hidden="false">
          <description>You may include 1-3 Tomb Spyders as a single Heavy Support choice, but Tomb Spyders are deployed as a single unit but do not have to be placed together and operate as independent units during the game.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink id="90fe-224b-ba35-5368" name="Heavy Support" hidden="false" targetId="9260-7d57-be5c-bd52" primary="true" />
      </categoryLinks>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry id="6c61-378b-e6c1-13dd" name="Tomb Spyder" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="model">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="3" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="fe7a-1a6e-ad7a-43eb" type="max" />
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="f693-8c31-813e-9ba9" type="min" />
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="ad9d-0017-5908-d99a" name="Hover" hidden="false">
              <description>Tomb Spyders move by gravitic propulsion but far more ponderously than airborne Necrons like Destroyers. They move and assault in the same manner as models on foot, even though they hover low above the ground.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule id="e3fb-750e-878d-14c4" name="Artificier" hidden="false">
              <description>Each Necron turn, at the start of the Assault phase, a Tomb Spyder that is not in close combat can expend energy to create a Scarab Swarm, The swarm is placed in contact with the Spuder at the start of the Assault phase. Roll D6 for each swarm produced. On a 1, the Spyder takes a wound. Each swarm produced will form a unit with the Tomb Spyder that created it and must retain coherency with it for the remainder of the game. Swarms produced this way are not worth any victory points and are removed if the Tomb Sypder is destroyed.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule id="a83f-3790-e563-b412" name="Necron Repair" hidden="false">
              <description>A Necron model may still self-repair if they would not normally be able due to distance to a similar model if they are within 12" of a Tomb Spyder and a unit they would be able to join is anywhere on the table. If the Necron repairs it will immediately join that model's unit.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink id="58a2-aabc-da02-de4c" name="Monstorous Creature" hidden="false" targetId="445e-e873-2a3f-776f" type="rule" />
            <infoLink id="1d4d-427c-b715-8e9b" name="Fearless" hidden="false" targetId="b137-13a1-eb97-c5e5" type="rule" />
            <infoLink id="3f50-b136-89ce-34d9" name="Tomb Spyder" hidden="false" targetId="f746-4c0b-3966-cd99" type="profile" />
          </infoLinks>
          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry id="e532-e868-af02-96f3" name="Particle Projector" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="de0e-c684-cb91-c1f3" type="max" />
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule id="5582-11f1-7f58-cc89" name="Particle Projector" hidden="false">
                  <description>Reduce the Spyder's number of Attacks by one.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <infoLinks>
                <infoLink id="73b3-219b-9447-0f1a" name="Staff of Light" hidden="false" targetId="f0e1-c7e2-18e3-5e45" type="profile">
                  <modifiers>
                    <modifier type="set" field="name" value="Particle Projector" />
                  </modifiers>
                </infoLink>
